<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30204" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγκατα-τίθημι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lay</i> or <i>put in</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">&lt;ἔν&gt; τινι τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orph.
					<u>H.</u>
					25.9
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐριχθόνιον . . νηῷ ἐγκατέθηκε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					14.1389i
				</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				i31
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> only in 
				Med.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱμάντα τεῷ ἐγκάτθεο κόλπῳ</span>
			<i>put</i> the band <i>upon</i> or <i>round</i> thy waist,
				<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				14.219
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				223
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄτην ἑῷ ἐγκάτθετο θυμῷ</span>
			<i>stored up, devised</i> mischief <i>in</i> his heart, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				23.223
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τελαμῶνα ἑῇ ἐγκάτθετο τέχνῃ</span>
			<i>stored up</i> the belt in his art, <i>designed</i> it by his
			art, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				11.614
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σὺ ταῦτα τεῷ ἐνικάτθεο θυμῷ</span>
			<i>store it</i> up <i>in</i> thy heart, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				27
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στέρνοις ἐγκατέθεντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Simon.
					85.5
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅκα φρεσὶν ἐγκατάθοιτο βουλάν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					17.14
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλυφίδας . . ἐνικάτθετο νευρῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					3.282
				</span></i>
			.</div>
